=== search/Provides search capability for the data set with the given search criteria.yml
info:
  name: Provides search capability for the data set with the given search criteria
  type: http
  seq: 1
  tags:
    - search

http:
  method: POST
  url: "{{baseUrl}}/:dataset/:version/records"
  params:
    - name: version
      value: v1
      type: path
      description: Version of the dataset.
    - name: dataset
      value: oa_citations
      type: path
      description: Name of the dataset. In this case, the default value is oa_citations
  body:
    type: form-urlencoded
    data:
      - name: criteria
        value: "*:*"
        description: "Uses Lucene Query Syntax in the format of propertyName:value, propertyName:[num1 TO num2] and date range format: propertyName:[yyyyMMdd TO yyyyMMdd]. In the response please see the 'docs' element which has the list of record objects. Each record structure would consist of all the fields and their corresponding values."
      - name: start
        value: "0"
        description: Starting record number. Default value is 0.
      - name: rows
        value: "100"
        description: Specify number of rows to be returned. If you run the search with default values, in the response you will see 'numFound' attribute which will tell the number of records available in the dataset.
  auth: inherit

settings:
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: inherit
  followRedirects: true
  maxRedirects: 5
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false

examples:
  - name: 200 Response
    description: successful operation
    request:
      url: "{{baseUrl}}/:dataset/:version/records"
      method: POST
      params:
        - name: version
          value: v1
          type: path
          description: Version of the dataset.
        - name: dataset
          value: oa_citations
          type: path
          description: Name of the dataset. In this case, the default value is oa_citations
      body:
        type: form-urlencoded
        data:
          - name: criteria
            value: "*:*"
            description: "Uses Lucene Query Syntax in the format of propertyName:value, propertyName:[num1 TO num2] and date range format: propertyName:[yyyyMMdd TO yyyyMMdd]. In the response please see the 'docs' element which has the list of record objects. Each record structure would consist of all the fields and their corresponding values."
          - name: start
            value: "0"
            description: Starting record number. Default value is 0.
          - name: rows
            value: "100"
            description: Specify number of rows to be returned. If you run the search with default values, in the response you will see 'numFound' attribute which will tell the number of records available in the dataset.
    response:
      status: 200
      statusText: OK
      headers:
        - name: Content-Type
          value: application/json
      body:
        type: json
        data: |-
          [
            {}
          ]

docs: This API is based on Solr/Lucene Search. The data is indexed using SOLR. This GET API returns the list of all the searchable field names that are in the Solr Index. Please see the 'fields' attribute which returns an array of field names. Each field or a combination of fields can be searched using the Solr/Lucene Syntax. Please refer https://lucene.apache.org/core/3_6_2/queryparsersyntax.html#Overview for the query syntax. List of field names that are searchable can be determined using above GET api.

